# THE MEASURED EXEMPLAR FRONTIER — where each of ticket 25's exemplars stops today.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# `examples/exemplars/README.md` used to answer this question in prose, and the
# prose rotted in the one direction nobody watches: the compiler got BETTER and
# the record did not follow. F13 landed binary patterns on 2026-08-20 and 25c
# stopped needing them — its wall moved from `consume.bs:14` on `<` to
# `consume.bs:20` on a destructure-and-bind pattern — while every gate stayed
# green, because no gate had ever compiled these files. The README says so
# itself: "`--check` catches the extracted files going stale against the
# prototypes; nothing catches the prototypes going stale against the *language*."
# This is that missing check's data.
#
# HOW TO READ A RECORD
# One record per directory under `compiler/examples/exemplars/`, tab-separated:
#
#     <directory>  <file>  <first diagnostic, path and line number removed>
#
# A directory that compiles clean is recorded as:
#
#     <directory>  -  clean
#
# The construct is pinned, NOT the line number. These files are regenerated from
# the write-ups by `extract-exemplars.sh`, so a sentence added to a prototype
# shifts every line below it; a gate that fired on that would be muted inside a
# week. `error: syntax error before: '=>'` is the claim worth defending.
#
# HOW TO CHANGE IT
# Do not hand-edit a record to make the gate green. Run
# `compiler/bin/check-exemplar-frontier.sh --update`, read the diff, and say in
# the commit message WHICH capability moved the wall. A record moving forward is
# the good news this gate exists to make visible — F13 earned it and nobody
# noticed for a day.
#
# WHAT A WALL IS NOT
# It is not a ranked list of everything an exemplar still needs. `bsc` stops at
# the first error, so a wall hides the ones behind it; the walls measured behind
# these three on 2026-08-21 are written up in README.md under "Behind the wall".
# A record moving forward means the front wall fell, never that the file is done.

25a-http-api-server	create_order.bs	error: illegal characters "#"
25b-websocket-handler	encode.bs	error: syntax error before: '=>'
25c-event-queue-consumer	encode.bs	error: syntax error before: '<<'
25d-database-querying	-	error: this directory holds `.bs` files and no `module` line
